{"id": "EUVD-2026-103964", "enisaUuid": "25fd88ba-13d5-32b1-bdea-83fdad91d628", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nwifi: iwlegacy: 3945: free EEPROM data on remove\n\nil3945_pci_probe() calls il_eeprom_init(), which allocates memory for\nthe EEPROM data. The probe failure paths release this allocation with\nil_eeprom_free(), but the remove path does not free it after a\nsuccessful probe.\n\nAs a result, the EEPROM data is leaked when the PCI device is removed.\n\nFree the EEPROM data in il3945_pci_remove() before releasing the\nmac80211 hardware structure.\n\nThis issue was found by manual code inspection.", "datePublished": "2026-10-18T15:46:40", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-21T12:55:59", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/3ebc529726c0c038f49e513a7a6f1893552ee803", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/ab7bee2cd55f665cb29fa0ace2ec14020e0a452e", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/cd8f8f45d81aac384311701d7ffe26567af2e783", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/89f9d6186dc7429f38132635526e28549c913c0b", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/f8ebe286394c0bbb4a6dbacb182a34ab6376922d"], "aliases": ["GHSA-8m9r-p559-452q", "CVE-2026-98710"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.17, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "38fb9514-d401-3342-b019-0d5666bec84f", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "073d3f5f1b3b6512eb82a3d40c84dedb14dc6f73 <89f9d6186dc7429f38132635526e28549c913c0b"}, {"id": "39dde5bc-0f2e-3b66-bf54-0f927d5a2e20", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.10"}, {"id": "4bfcf3a0-51f3-33f5-bc0c-6beb91507c20", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.6.160"}, {"id": "518e0dd7-71de-36e7-96b9-38f9ff4d74e7", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.56"}, {"id": "629ac60c-f4be-35f9-9e87-14f9eb8be555", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"n